//! GENERATED by the milestone-11 golden capture -- do not hand-edit.
//!
//! Every value below is the reference engine's own output, produced by slicing
//! script block 4 out of the frozen `reference/Cartalith Gen1 v2.10.html` and
//! running it under node. The capture asserts, before it runs anything: both
//! block markers, both `<script>` tags, the FIRST LINE of all six milestone-11
//! functions, that line 30190 is `lanePass`'s `return added;}`, that line 30193
//! is `buildBlocks` (so the slice ends where it should), and that the block
//! comments inside the slice balance. The six functions are added to `UME`'s
//! export by a single anchored replacement of the `_test:` line, asserted to
//! match exactly once. The frozen file itself is never written.
//!
//! [`Scenario::hash`] is the reference's OWN `fnv1a` over a canonical dump of
//! the whole graph: every node's id, position (x100, integer) and adjacency
//! list **in order**, then every edge's id, endpoints, class, width (x10,
//! integer), epoch and liveness. Integers only, so JS and Rust cannot disagree
//! on float formatting. Adjacency order is in the hash because `kill_edge`'s
//! whole job is to splice those lists.
//!
//! The capture asserts each scenario left a non-empty node list, a non-empty
//! edge list and at least one LIVE edge before writing, and that across the set
//! at least one scenario killed an edge, one laid a lane, one cleared a parcel,
//! one removed a building and one removed a detail. A silently-empty golden is
//! this project's most-repeated failure.

